
=== G1: backup vs deletion + dump contents ================================
AUDIT|G1.backup-profile-config|BLOCKED|compose backup profile: pg_dump=True, 35-day retention=yes, AES-256-CBC/PBKDF2-600k dump encryption with the key REQUIRED via the mounted secret file (env-fallback line=True, BACKUP_KEY_FILE mount=True, secrets: entry=True, shared helper=True, -iter pin=True) — a stolen backup volume is ciphertext at rest and a missing key refuses the dump outright. Residual by design: dumps taken before a deletion still hold the user's rows until retention expires; the README states this as the deletion-and-retention scope
AUDIT|G1.dump-contents|INFO|what a dump carries (same columns): 0 usernames, 0 entries, 0 distinct dates, blob sizes (None, None, None) — with the 2026-09-16 fix this metadata is only readable by a BACKUP_KEY holder (AES-256-CBC at rest); the residual is the retention-vs-deletion window, not plaintext-on-disk

